{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise VALIDATED against current main, with a sharper mechanism than filed for the probe test.\n\n**Seam 1 — Jira capability retry.** `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py:44` declared `sleep_fn=time.sleep`, evaluated once at import. The filed claim is that the test's `mock.patch(\"time.sleep\")  # avoid real delay` therefore misses. Measured, and it is order-dependent:\n\n| run | duration |\n|---|---|\n| `test_probe_retries_jql_search_three_times` ALONE | **0.01s** |\n| same test as part of its module | **25.01s** |\n\nAlone, the probe module is first imported INSIDE the active `mock.patch`, so the default captures the mock. Within the module, `test_probe_round_trip_passes_all_six_steps` imports `access_check` first, outside any patch, so the default captures the real `time.sleep` and the JQL loop sleeps 5 x `JQL_RETRY_SLEEP=5` = 25s. That is the filed 25.3s, and it explains why the defect is invisible to a focused re-run — a real trap for anyone trying to reproduce it.\n\n**Seam 2 — dependency audit.** `scripts/dependency_audit.py:194`, same `sleeper = time.sleep` shape; `test_gate_reports_db_unreachable_as_infrastructure` measured **15.00s** (`attempt * 5` for attempts 1 and 2).\n\n**Seam 3 — stale-binding 500.** `test_non_404_http_error_still_propagates` patched nothing at all and drove `_call_with_retry`'s real ADR-0036 backoff (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:129`, `2**(attempt+1) + jitter`): measured **16.18s**.\n\nAll three premises hold. Total measured waste: **56.19s** of pure wall clock across three unit tests."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786604637076901001,"uuid":"c9b414e2-217f-4ef0-9721-93b84d7cde71"}